        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 81,
        "headingId": 540,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8051/3 Verrucous carcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:54:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 502,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 541,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69625,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 81,
        "headingId": 541,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C9Y &amp; XH5PM0 Other specified malignant neoplasms of urinary tract &amp; Verrucous carcinoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:54:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 503,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 542,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69626,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 81,
        "headingId": 542,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:54:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 504,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 543,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69627,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 81,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:54:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69628,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 81,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most cases of verrucous carcinoma occur in the bladder {30565306; 2033707}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:54:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69629,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 81,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients often present with haematuria, dysuria, urinary frequency, or obstructive symptoms {30565306; 15257362; 6415887}. Urinary excretion of cellular debris has also been reported {8351470}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:54:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69630,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 81,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Verrucous carcinoma most commonly occurs in areas where schistosomiasis is endemic {8351470; 30565306}, although it has also been reported in patients from other areas {10738227}. It is seen more frequently in men, often in the fifth decade of life {30565306; 8351470}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:54:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69631,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 81,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Verrucous carcinoma of the bladder is most often seen in the setting of schistosomiasis, with a reported incidence of 5000&nbsp;cases per 100&nbsp;000&nbsp;person-years in endemic areas {7306921; 30565306}. Rare sporadic cases from areas without endemic schistosomiasis have been reported {15257362; 10738227}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:54:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69632,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 81,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most verrucous carcinoma occurs in patients with schistosomiasis {7306921}, although a few cases unrelated to schistosomiasis have also been reported {16819332}. HPV infection is not associated with carcinogenesis {16819332; 15257362}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:54:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69633,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 81,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Grossly, these tumours appear as exophytic, fungating lesions that are typically solitary.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:54:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69634,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 81,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "<p>These tumours have the same histological features as those that arise in other areas of the body, including warty gross features, large hyperkeratotic papillae, and acanthosis with minimal cytological atypia. They have a broad, pushing, invasive front, with tongue-like downward projections. Mitoses are rare. This is different from the classic small, irregular invasive tumour nests with paradoxical maturation seen in typical squamous cell carcinoma of the bladder {30565306; 2033707}.</p>\r\n<p>The diagnosis of verrucous carcinoma requires examination of the entire lesion to rule out the presence of conventional invasive squamous carcinomas.</p>\r\n<p>Focal cytoplasmic and membranous positivity for EGFR and TGF-&alpha; have been reported {9828815}, as has increased p53 expression {10738227}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-04-01T12:06:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69635,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 81,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not available</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:54:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69636,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 81,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:54:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69637,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 81,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a warty mass on gross examination; histology shows verrucous or papillary growth, minimal nuclear and architectural atypia, and rounded and pushing deep borders.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:54:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69638,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 81,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Staging is based on the American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) and Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM system. Most cases are categorized as stage&nbsp;I.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:54:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 69639,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 81,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Verrucous carcinoma has classically been considered a clinically indolent tumour. Most cases have been reported to have an excellent clinical prognosis. Rarely, it may be locally aggressive; extravesical extension and transformation to invasive squamous cell carcinoma have been reported {7815602; 8351470}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-10T18:54:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]